  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Finland pre-departure orientation programme 2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will prepare approximately 500 quota refugees for resettlement and early integration in Finland. IOM will provide three-day, in-person pre-departure orientation training to around 450 beneficiaries from Iran, Peru, Rwanda and T&#xfc;rkiye. Where possible, approximately 50 beneficiaries selected worldwide under Finland&apos;s unallocated or emergency quota will receive a one-day remote orientation or written materials. The training will strengthen participants&apos; practical skills and knowledge of Finnish society and language through age-, gender- and context-sensitive support. IOM will also update self-study resources, including the &quot;Moving to Finland&quot; website, to support continued learning.</narrative>
  </description>
